{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"@'\nReviewed: 9da666cbf8200e0e93c8efdddecc5c26c741cbf8\n\nVerified: Reviewed the scoped three-dot diff against WI-993 and its complete spec of record, the quoted owner rulings, PROCESS sections 3/5/6, cited registry rows and kit-change-review anchors. Hunted silent loss of owner-held work first, then incorrect readiness, unintended amendment suppression and replay duplication. The shipped mint creates the owner row, pending item, citation and watermark together; the shared queue surfaces claimed citers. No reachable fail-open or data-loss defect was found. The targeted run had two failures, both reproduced on the base revision; all new held-act and claimed-citer cases passed. One normative wording conflict remains below. This is a code/content review, not approval of changed spine cells or an endorsement of an approval gate.\n\nCommands:\n\n- \"'`git rev-parse HEAD` -> `9da666cbf8200e0e93c8efdddecc5c26c741cbf8`.\n- `Get-Content CLAUDE.md`, the antidote/session-protocol/coordinator-cycle skills, WI-993'\"'s full active spec, \"'`docs/specs/WI-993.md`, and `docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md`; targeted `Get-Content` ranges and `rg` searches of PROCESS, cited registry rows, changed code/tests and their immediate dependencies -> established the owner ruling, intake route, threat bound and contract relationships. Registry reads were scoped to matching rows; no whole registry or session log was read. The first registry glob search was rejected by Windows; the corrected `rg ... docs/requirements -g '\"'*.toml'\"'` supplied the targeted matches.\n- `git diff 0c5fc7696323994ca9ceb238a735d927792c77b0...9da666cbf8200e0e93c8efdddecc5c26c741cbf8 -- . '\"':(exclude)docs/iteration' ':(exclude)docs/reviews' ':(exclude)docs/log.md' ':(exclude)docs/log.d' ':(exclude)PROJECT_STATE.html' ':(exclude)docs/open-items.html' ':(exclude)docs/sta