ged; the extra snapshot probe verifies the owner's later act settles it.\n- No child decomposition was introduced. Retained LLR-118 independently specifies rendering, LLR-299 citation integrity, LLR-153 mint allocation/routing and LLR-364 settlement evidence. Each has a distinct observable decision or verification purpose. Splitting their changed clauses further would partition a single existing output/decision rather than add an independent requirement. New helpers perform distinct acceptance lookup, verdict selection, held-row grouping and brief construction; existing item writing, allocation, queue projection and row comparison are reused.\n\nFindings:\n\n- [MINOR] docs/requirements/interfaces.toml:1042 -> for clarity [K1]: IF-073 now includes claimed citers but still requires every ruling to add a Done-when criterion citing the item; the new registry/template instructions instead require a planned claimed citer to tick its existing item and add no evidence, and that route passes ruling-sync while preserving its digest -> qualify IF-073's ruling sentence with the planned-claimed-step exception, matching docs/requirements/open-items.toml:30 and project-trajectory/registries/open-items.template.toml:41 -> @implementer\nVERDICT: CHANGES-REQUESTED findings=1\n'@ | Set-Content -Encoding utf8 -LiteralPath C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-06-leg34/s1A/wi-993-9da666c-full-review.md\nGet-Content -LiteralPath C:/Projects/ai-template.wt/review-tmp/2026-11-06-leg34/s1A/wi-993-9da666c-full-review.md -TotalCount 1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
